ABSTRACT:
we give general conditions to state a weighted hardy inequality \[ c\int_{\mathbb{r}^n} rac{\varphi^2} {|x|^2}d\mu\leq\int_{\mathbb{r}^n}|
abla \varphi |^2 d\mu+c\int_{\mathbb{r}^n} \varphi^2d\mu,\quad \varphi\in c_c^{\infty}(\mathbb{r}^n),\,c\leq c_{0,\mu}, \] with respect to the probability measure $d\mu$. moreover, a optimality of a constant $c_{0,\mu}$ was given. a inequality was related to a following kolmogorov equation perturbed by the singular potential \[ lu+vu=\left(\delta u+ rac{
