we investigate how a dark energy properties change a cosmological limits on sterile neutrino parameters by with the help of recent cosmological observations. we consider a simplest dynamical dark energy models, a $w$cdm model and a holographic dark energy (hde) model, to make an analysis. a cosmological observations used inside this work include a planck 2015 cmb temperature and polarization data, a baryon acoustic oscillation data, a type ia supernova data, a hubble constant direct measurement data, and a planck cmb lensing data. we find that, $m_{
u,{m{sterile}}}^{m{eff}}<0.2675$ ev and $n_{m eff}<3.5718$ considering $\lambda$cdm cosmology, $m_{
u,{m{sterile}}}^{m{eff}}<0.5313$ ev and $n_{m eff}<3.5008$ considering $w$cdm cosmology, and $m_{
u,{m{sterile}}}^{m{eff}}<0.1989$ ev and $n_{m eff}<3.6701$ considering hde cosmology, from a constraints of a combination of these data. thus, without a addition of measurements of growth of structure, only upper limits on both $m_{
u,{m{sterile}}}^{m{eff}}$ and $n_{m eff}$ should be derived, indicating that no evidence of a existence of the sterile neutrino species with ev-scale mass was found inside this analysis. moreover, compared to a $\lambda$cdm model, inside a $w$cdm model a limit on $m_{
u,{m{sterile}}}^{m{eff}}$ becomes much looser, but inside a hde model a limit becomes much tighter. therefore, a dark energy properties could significantly influence a constraint limits of sterile neutrino parameters.

